# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.1
# ignores vulnerabilities until expiry date; change duration by modifying expiry date
ignore:
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGJETBRAINSKOTLIN-2393744:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2020-29582: This vulnerability relates to information exposure via
          creation of temporary files (via Kotlin functions) with insecure
          permissions. Corda does not use any of the vulnerable functions so it
          not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T01:00:00.000Z
        created: 2024-05-30T10:37:19.923Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGGRADLE-5750785:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2023-35947: This is a build-related vulnerability that does not
          affect the running of Corda. The Gradle build for Corda does not
          unpack any TAR archives. Corda is not exposed to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T01:00:00.000Z
        created: 2024-05-30T10:37:24.413Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGGLASSFISHJAXB-20883142:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-92877: This vulnerability relates to XML External Entity
          (XXE) injection when JAXB unmarshals untrusted XML. jaxb-core reaches
          Corda only through hibernate-core 7.4.12.Final. Corda has no JAXB code
          and bootstraps Hibernate from annotated classes without mapping XML;
          Hibernate unmarshals any mapping XML from a StAX reader it configures
          itself, so JAXB's own parser is never used, and the only path that lets
          JAXB parse input directly, Hibernate's JaxbXmlFormatMapper, is used
          only for XML-typed columns, which Corda does not have. Corda is
          therefore not susceptible to this vulnerability. No fixed version has
          been released yet (expected in jaxb 4.0.10); upgrade and remove this
          entry when it is.
        expires: 2027-01-31T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-22T14:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGJETBRAINSKOTLIN-2628385:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2022-24329: This vulnerability relates to the Kotlin Multiplatform
          Gradle plugin not locking dependencies before Kotlin 1.6.0, a build-time
          issue. Kotlin 1.2.71 is used only as the runtime of the external verifier
          (core-1.2, serialization-1.2, verifier) and of the 4.11 test CorDapps,
          because contracts built for Corda 4.11 and earlier need the Kotlin 1.2
          runtime. Nothing is built with the Multiplatform plugin. Corda is
          therefore not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T01:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-22T14:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-JAKARTAVALIDATION-20936881:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          This vulnerability relates to Validation.byProvider dropping the
          caller's ProtectionDomain in AccessController.doPrivileged, so it can
          only be exploited when the JVM runs with a SecurityManager. Corda runs on
          JDK 17 and never installs a SecurityManager, and does not bootstrap Bean
          Validation (jakarta.validation-api arrives with jersey-server). The only
          fixed version is the 4.0.0-M1 milestone, which Jersey 3.1 does not
          support. Corda is therefore not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2027-11-22T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-22T14:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
